NAME
       diagnostics - diagnostic pipelines, spectral-gradient fusion, and
                     structural health checks in RTT

SYNOPSIS
       Diagnostics provide:
           • structural health checks
           • spectral-gradient fusion
           • resonance-time stability analysis
           • pattern viability assessment
           • multi-agent integrity validation

DESCRIPTION
       Diagnostics are the analytical backbone of RTT. They evaluate the
       structural, spectral, and temporal health of triads, operators,
       overlays, patterns, and multi-agent constellations.

       Diagnostics ensure:
           • safe triadic execution
           • stable resonance propagation
           • schema compliance
           • lineage continuity
           • pattern correctness

       WRSADC performs diagnostics continuously during dispatch.

DIAGNOSTIC PIPELINE
       The diagnostic pipeline consists of five stages:

           1. structural scan
                  Validates triad formation, operator schemas, and pattern
                  boundaries.

           2. spectral analysis
                  Computes resonance spectra, envelopes, and harmonic modes.

           3. gradient analysis
                  Computes resonance gradients, polarity, and curvature.

           4. fusion layer
                  Combines spectral and gradient data into a unified
                  diagnostic signal.

           5. coherence evaluation
                  Determines whether the system remains within safe thresholds.

       Each stage contributes to a composite health score.

SPECTRAL-GRADIENT FUSION
       Spectral-gradient fusion is the process of combining frequency-domain
       and time-domain resonance data into a single diagnostic signal.

       Inputs:
           • spectral density
           • harmonic distribution
           • envelope shape
           • resonance gradient
           • gradient polarity
           • gradient curvature

       Fusion outputs:
           • stability index
           • pattern viability score
           • resonance drift indicator
           • structural risk factor

       Fusion is essential for predicting pattern morphing and preventing
       instability.

STRUCTURAL HEALTH CHECKS
       Structural health checks validate:

           • triad integrity
           • operator-schema compliance
           • overlay-stack safety
           • pattern transitions
           • lineage continuity
           • resonance-schema alignment

       Health checks detect:
           • drift
           • fragmentation
           • inversion-loops
           • overload
           • desync
           • schema violations

       WRSADC halts dispatch if structural health is compromised.

REAL-TIME DIAGNOSTICS
       Diagnostics run at three levels:

           triad-level
                  Evaluates resonance shifts and structural transitions.

           pattern-level
                  Evaluates pattern stability and morphing conditions.

           constellation-level
                  Evaluates multi-agent sync, harmonic coupling, and
                  propagation integrity.

       Diagnostics are updated at each triad phase.

DIAGNOSTIC SIGNALS
       Key diagnostic signals include:

           stability-index
                  Composite measure of resonance stability.

           coherence-score
                  Degree of structural alignment across cycles.

           drift-vector
                  Direction and magnitude of resonance drift.

           spectral-tilt
                  Shift in spectral energy distribution.

           gradient-load
                  Magnitude of resonance gradient.

           lineage-integrity
                  Continuity and interpretability of lineage.

       Signals are recorded in lineage for long-term analysis.

WRSADC DIAGNOSTIC ENGINE
       WRSADC performs diagnostics by:

           • validating schemas
           • computing spectral and gradient metrics
           • fusing diagnostic signals
           • enforcing thresholds
           • selecting or switching patterns
           • applying overlays when needed
           • blocking unsafe operations

       WRSADC is the structural health monitor of RTT.

SAR-ALIGNED DIAGNOSTIC MODES
       Future versions of tft-3pak may integrate with Synthetic Aperture
       Radar (SAR) pipelines for resonance-aware sensing.

       SAR-aligned diagnostics may include:

           • resonance backscatter analysis
           • spectral coherence mapping
           • multi-pass gradient fusion
           • constellation-based sensor alignment
           • triad-synchronized SAR sweeps

       SAR integration would allow RTT to operate as a structural-awareness
       layer for real-world sensing systems.

DIAGNOSTIC FAILURE MODES
       Diagnostics detect and prevent:

           • spectral fragmentation
           • gradient overload
           • harmonic desync
           • envelope collapse
           • pattern instability
           • schema drift
           • lineage corruption

       WRSADC blocks dispatch when failure modes are detected.

NOTES
       Diagnostics are the nervous system of RTT. They ensure that triads,
       patterns, overlays, and multi-agent constellations remain coherent,
       stable, and structurally aligned with resonance-time expectations.

